first our top story this hour a  temporary ceasefire proposed by the  russians was expected to go into effect  this morning in ukraine the plan would  have allowed civilians safe passage out  of two parts of the country but now the  effort appears to be on hold as russia  russia's shelling continues and it  follows another explosive night across  much of the country the united nations  estimates as many as 4 million people  could be displaced in the coming weeks  that's about 10 percent of the  population many are fleeing to  neighboring poland where they are being  welcomed with no required paperwork  christina raffini is at a border  crossing in poland christina good  morning  good morning we're at the kachova border  crossing between poland and ukraine  where it's snowing and freezing and all  morning we've seen lines of refugees  waiting out in the cold to board buses  to refugee receiving centers other  places in poland now we've seen a lot of  mothers we've seen children that's  because military-aged men are not  allowed to leave the country and more  families are having to make the  heartbreaking decision to separate  saying last goodbyes through train  station gates or windows now secretary  of state lincoln landed in poland this  morning he was in brussels yesterday  where he was asked if nato would  consider instituting a no-fly zone over  ukraine lincoln said the only way to  enforce that would be put u.s and nato  planes in a face-off situation with  russian fighters and he said president  biden has been clear we are not going to  get in a war with russia now what the  u.s has done is send thousands of troops  to reinforce nato allies like poland  yesterday we visited an airstrip on the  side of a rural road where the 82nd  airborne has heavy equipment and is  setting up a temporary base of  operations just one of the many around  here as the u.s tries to reassure nato  allies it has their backs now people  here in poland are nervous yesterday  poland's ambassador to ukraine said he  doesn't think kev will fall because  there are a lot of people on the street  he wouldn't want to meet if he were a  russian however he said if ukraine does  fall poland could be next michelle  christina thank you
 

